     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is 5 times the usual maximum dose.** The labeled maximum for adults is 200 mg/day. Most adults start at 25\u201350 mg daily and increase to 50\u2013200 mg daily. A dose of 1000 mg is in overdose territory and raises the risk of serotonin syndrome and QT prolongation.\n\nThis may be a typo for **100 mg**, which is a common maintenance dose. Can you tell me which you meant?\n\n1. **Sertraline 100 mg PO once daily.** I'll enter it as written.\n2. **A different dose**, such as 50 mg or 200 mg.\n3. **1000 mg is intended.** If so, please confirm and give the clinical reason. I'd also recommend checking with pharmacy before it's dispensed.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
